Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: propagate Uke Xiaomi status events

The Uke OEM handle_notification() reports a battery change for notification
payload 0x50; the shared Xiaomi GLINK implementation in Peridot does likewise.
The Uke queue currently discards this payload, preventing event-driven battery
consumers from observing vendor status changes until another event or poll.

Route the validated Uke notification through the existing battery event path.
Keep raw opcode 0x50 messages, reply matching and charger controls unchanged.
This notification is not a bypass-state or electrical-isolation indication.

References: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd,
drivers/power/supply/qti_battery_charger.c; redzrush101/linux
2ed9eadbecae21ef51134e556951e7305ba65f88, drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c.
Original GPL-2.0-only Linux Foundation/Linaro/Qualcomm attribution is retained.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1686,7 +1686,7 @@
 	notification = le32_to_cpu(msg->notification);
 	notification &= 0xff;
 	if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE && notification == 0x50)
-		return;
+		notification = NOTIF_BAT_PROPERTY;
 	switch (notification) {
 	case NOTIF_BAT_INFO:
 		battmgr->info.valid = false;
